These are the primary sources the csoh.org kill chain cites. Every fact about the incident in this deck comes from that page, which draws on these.

Codecov's security update is its own account of the incident. GitGuardian and CyberArk each break the attack down, and the CyberArk link is an archived copy. CNCF TAG Security, part of the Cloud Native Computing Foundation, keeps a catalog entry for the compromise. The MITRE page defines T1195.002, Compromise Software Supply Chain, the technique behind stage 02. Mercari's incident report is its own account of what the uploader exposed.

The background slides name their own sources: OWASP, the csoh.org glossary, and two RFCs.

