The page calls Codecov the direct ancestor of the LiteLLM / Trivy compromise. The four topics are its related defense topics.
notes:
The page links three other kill chains, and four defense topics.

It calls Codecov the direct ancestor of the LiteLLM / Trivy compromise five years later. It says the hash pinning that would have caught npm debug/chalk was available, cheap, and skipped. And it says constraining runner egress breaks the exfiltration step in Codecov, Megalodon and LiteLLM alike.

The page's related defense topics are CI/CD security, container security, non-human identity and GitHub Actions. CI/CD stands for continuous integration and continuous delivery.
